00:24:13,040 --> 00:24:17,440
And they are a combination of an app and a physical product, a tracker that you can put on your dog.

252
00:24:17,920 --> 00:24:24,160
I have a half husky, which anyone who has a husky or knows huskies well know that they are notorious for running away.

253
00:24:24,800 --> 00:24:25,840
My dog likes to run away.

254
00:24:26,320 --> 00:24:36,000
And I saw a million of their ads, but all their ads were 35% off on dog and cat trackers, GPS and health trackers.

255
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:42,800
It's like if your ad is just saying, get this, this cow, this is what we do, that's not speaking to someone's job to be done.

256
00:24:43,360 --> 00:24:50,400
But then I read one of their reviews and it was about this Siberian husky that had run off and the owner was so grateful she had tractor.

257
00:24:50,560 --> 00:24:57,280
It gave her so much peace of mind because the dog literally got in a car with a stranger who was trying to find their owner.

258
00:24:57,600 --> 00:24:58,480
They weren't stealing it.

259
00:24:58,640 --> 00:25:15,040
They were literally just driving around and the owner could follow this car for fifteen minutes to the vet that they decided like, okay, let's just bring the dog here until we can work out, you know, with maybe the microchip that's running and they could get their dog back and just literally follow a dog on having this little ride along with a random stranger.

260
00:25:15,600 --> 00:25:28,240
And like, I was like, if I saw an ad showing this, I would have bought this years ago, but it took me losing my dog for the tenth time and multiple people telling me, you're like, you're an idiot trying to fix this with an AirTag.

261
00:25:28,480 --> 00:25:29,600
You keep losing your dog.

262
00:25:30,320 --> 00:25:38,080
Either you don't let him lose or you put him on, you know, or you get a better tracker for me to realize this was the solution I needed.

263
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:39,840
And so I could have bought it five years ago.

264
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:45,360
They could have had so much more money for me if I'd realized that I just didn't know that I needed a GPS tracker.

265
00:25:45,600 --> 00:25:46,800
I didn't think that was the solution.

266
00:25:47,040 --> 00:25:48,800
I spent ages trying to train my dog.

267
00:25:48,800 --> 00:25:54,560
I spent ages trying to find alternative ways of doing it with long leashes, with using an AirTag.

268
00:25:55,120 --> 00:26:08,960
But I just didn't process that GPS tracker would work so much better until I actually lost my dog again and I just followed him through the forest on this little wander around until I could get him back on leash and be like, okay, you've lost walk and loose duty.

269
00:26:09,360 --> 00:26:16,880
So I think like trying to bring to life that journey, either the start of the journey or where they can be, is one of the most powerful ad formats out there.

270
00:26:16,960 --> 00:26:20,160
And there's a reason why Ladder, who you're right, are crushing it.

