00:27:15,120 --> 00:27:16,960
So CalAI is a great example.

280
00:27:17,360 --> 00:27:20,960
Like they've been blowing up lately and they pay a lot of influencers.

281
00:27:21,280 --> 00:27:23,280
There's a little bit of mixed messaging on Twitter.

282
00:27:23,920 --> 00:27:28,640
People act as if it's fully organic, but they actually pay a ton of creators to create this.

283
00:27:28,880 --> 00:27:33,680
So it's a different form of paid marketing when you pay UGC creators.

284
00:27:34,000 --> 00:27:53,360
And I think even they're putting money behind some of that as well their ads, the ads are brilliant because it's a TikTok like day in the life of or different things like I mean, there's so many different formats they've used, but one of the ones I saw, they just incorporated Cali AI into their normal routine.

285
00:27:53,600 --> 00:27:58,400
And so the job to be done is like, you know, wanting to track your food, but tracking your food is a hassle.

286
00:27:59,040 --> 00:28:08,400
And so they show them like going to a workout and then they're coming home and they're eating the meal and then they just take a photo of the meal and it tells you the calories and then they move on with their day.

287
00:28:08,720 --> 00:28:13,680
It's almost like it's not an ad because it's in passing that they just happen to show it.

288
00:28:13,920 --> 00:28:22,000
But it ends up being so compelling because we all know if you're trying to lose weight, you really should track your food, but tracking your food is a hassle.

289
00:28:22,160 --> 00:28:25,200
And they've, and to your point, what's the differentiation of CalAI?

290
00:28:25,520 --> 00:28:26,000
Take a picture.

291
00:28:26,560 --> 00:28:36,080
And so they're very, almost subtly working it into this TikTok that can go viral and get more attention because it's not an ad.

292
00:28:36,880 --> 00:28:44,320
But then they're showing the job to be done in such a powerful way because instead of it being this big hassle, pulling out the app and logging your food, you just take a picture.

293
00:28:44,640 --> 00:28:53,040
I think that's a great example of, you know, again, I don't think they would they didn't sit there down and think through the jobs to be done framework, but it works out that way.

294
00:28:53,520 --> 00:29:07,840
And by sitting down and thinking through the jobs to be done framework, you can start creating those kinds of ads that really do more directly show off the differentiation of the app and how it satisfies those jobs to be done in a better way.

295
00:29:08,320 --> 00:29:20,320
I think like if you like, we're like, okay, ignore the jobs to be done framework, a different way of almost thinking about it where you're deed doing this accidental thing, which sounds like they're doing is they've realized what that aha moment is.

296
00:29:20,960 --> 00:29:25,520
Like what is the moment that people realize this is something I need to achieve whatever they're trying to achieve.

297
00:29:26,000 --> 00:29:30,960
And they're just working out, like, how can I bring that forward in the journey and to help bring it across it.

298
00:29:31,200 --> 00:29:36,960
And the reason it's working is because it's talking to that job to be done of, like, hey, I want to be able to track it with ease.

299
00:29:37,680 --> 00:29:39,520
But it's just bringing that almost forward.

